  "goodToKnow": "Der Wachtmeister is an old rank for a police constable or a cavalry sergeant. In Germany it now sounds folksy, as in children's stories, though Justizwachtmeister still guard courtrooms. In Switzerland and Austria, Wachtmeister remains a real military or police rank. Die Wache means guard or police station: auf die Wache gehen. The plural is the same: die Wachtmeister."
